// BT-3047 / ADR 0109 amendment: a block-taking class method whose hierarchy
// does *not* define `foo` — pins the "confusing does_not_understand blaming
// the wrong class" half of the bug (fixtures/bt3047parent.bt hands this
// class a block containing `self foo`, inherited only from BT3047Ancestor;
// before the fix, resolving `self foo` against THIS class's hierarchy raised
// DNU here instead of running BT3047Ancestor's implementation).

Value subclass: BT3047DriverPlain

  // BT-3047: the block runs inside THIS class's own gen_server process
  // (ADR 0109), not the caller's.
  class run: aBlock :: Block over: aList :: List -> Nil =>
    aList do: [:x | aBlock value: x]
    nil
